<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><gpx xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:groundspeak="http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" version="1.0" creator="Groundspeak, Inc.All Rights Reserved.http://www.groundspeak.com" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0/gpx.xsd http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1 http://www.groundspeak.com/cache/1/0/1/cache.xsd" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/0"><name>Cache Listing Generated from Geocaching.com</name><desc>This is an individual cache generated from Geocaching.com</desc><email>contact@geocaching.com</email><url>http://www.geocaching.com</url><urlname>Geocaching - High Tech Treasure Hunting</urlname><time>2026-03-02T05:14:58.9569189Z</time><keywords>cache, geocache</keywords><wpt lat="39.426967" lon="-84.4253"><time>2011-04-18T00:00:00</time><name>GC2RNPW</name><desc>Watercolor mini-print #1 by Bimble Inc</desc><url>https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GC2RNPW</url><urlname>Watercolor mini-print #1</urlname><sym>Geocache</sym><type>Geocache|Traditional Cache</type><groundspeak:cache id="2171796" available="true" archived="false"><groundspeak:name>Watercolor mini-print #1</groundspeak:name><groundspeak:placed_by>Bimble Inc</groundspeak:placed_by><groundspeak:owner id="4244106">Bimble Inc</groundspeak:owner><groundspeak:type>Traditional Cache</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:container>Small</groundspeak:container><groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:attribute id="1" inc="1">Dogs</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="13" inc="0">Available 24/7</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="25" inc="1">Parking nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="55" inc="1">Short hike (&lt;1 km)</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="14" inc="0">Recommended at night</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="30" inc="1">Picnic tables nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="28" inc="1">Public restrooms nearby</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="15" inc="1">Available in winter</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="17" inc="1">Poisonous plants</groundspeak:attribute><groundspeak:attribute id="39" inc="1">Thorns</groundspeak:attribute></groundspeak:attributes><groundspeak:difficulty>2</groundspeak:difficulty><groundspeak:terrain>2.5</groundspeak:terrain><groundspeak:country>United States</groundspeak:country><groundspeak:state>Ohio</groundspeak:state><groundspeak:short_description>Thorn Tour of Liberty Township</groundspeak:short_description><groundspeak:long_description>Paths lead to a twisting maze of skeletal thorns and honeysuckle. Adventurer beware! Though you will not have to climb any mountains or cross any rushing rivers, a journey through these warrens is not for the faint of heart. Coming out wounded at the cache site could just lead to more trouble.

Yay! ghs was the first to survive.</groundspeak:long_description><groundspeak:encoded_hints>Spin in a clockwise circle three times, and mutter "counterclockwise". The cache will magically appear.</groundspeak:encoded_hints><groundspeak:logs><groundspeak:log id="1325058661"><groundspeak:date>2025-09-19T19:15:24</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="53815852">Cadurro5687</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">It wasn't anywhere to be found</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1319478058"><groundspeak:date>2025-08-22T12:44:26</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="53267836">sparkyjoe8181</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">Tftc</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1299642329"><groundspeak:date>2025-05-19T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="1148650">SM325</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">The Mighty Three were out for another weekly Zany Geocaching Adventure (ZGA) invading the cities of Springdale, Mount Heathy, Dent, Bridgetown and Delhi.

We parked on Bryson Lane and took the public sidewalk into the woods. As I am limited mobility, I used my power chair to reach GZ which was about 243 feet from the GeoMobile. All the neighborhood dogs began a barking chorus and I was proud of Tazzy as his training paid off and we did not hear a single noise from him. Once we reached GZ, my Geocaching partner searched for a few minutes and found the original container. We were only too happy to give this lonely geocache a little bit of love.

I read a few of the earlier logs and it appeared this was quite a bushwhacking debacle to reach this one. This is no longer true as the walk is extremely simple.

Thanks so much for putting this one out as well as feeding my insatiable addiction!  The log sheet was signed BTS for br549*, Tazzy and SM325.</groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1299464398"><groundspeak:date>2025-05-19T10:53:24</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="15369726">br549*</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false"> I am out with SM325 and Tazzy on todays adventure in geocaching. It is supposed to be nice today with a high in the 70’s.  We are knocking out a number of different types today. Our goal is to get 30 today. Thanks. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log><groundspeak:log id="1286377175"><groundspeak:date>2025-03-19T12:00:00</groundspeak:date><groundspeak:type>Didn't find it</groundspeak:type><groundspeak:finder id="2964911">BeeKind525</groundspeak:finder><groundspeak:text encoded="false">I was out taking a walk in this beautiful weather before the cold front comes in. I had my two younger children looking and we couldn't find it. We'll have to try another time. </groundspeak:text></groundspeak:log></groundspeak:logs></groundspeak:cache></wpt></gpx>